   "reply": "I added `Ledger.deposit(name, amount)` and `Ledger.withdraw(name, amount)` in `src/ledgerlite/__init__.py`, and the full suite passes (8 tests: the 2 existing and 6 new).\n\n- **`deposit`:** it adds the amount to the account. Like `transfer`, it takes the amount as a string and raises `ValueError` if the amount isn't positive.\n- **`withdraw`:** it raises `ValueError` if the amount isn't positive, or if it would take the account below zero. Withdrawing exactly the full balance is allowed. A refused withdrawal leaves the balance unchanged.\n- **Tests:** the new tests in `tests/test_ledger.py` cover each success case, the non-positive amounts, the exact-balance withdrawal, and an overdraw that leaves the balance untouched.\n\n`transfer` can still push the source account negative, because I didn't change it. Say so if you want it to enforce the same rule.",
